<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">River Feale</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The River Feale rises in the Mullaghareirk Mountains near the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a> and flows north-west through north Kerry, past Listowel, to the Shannon estuary near Ballybunion, Ireland. Part of its course forms the border between counties Limerick and Kerry. Its valley lay at the heart of the territory of the Ciarraige Luachra in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/river-feale.jpg" alt="River Feale" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Larsoner at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River_Feale_Finuge_Crossing_1.JPEG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
